{
  "title": "postern",
  "uid": "postern-agent",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "tags": [
    "postern",
    "spa",
    "break-glass"
  ],
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "instance",
        "label": "Host",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(postern_agent_info, instance)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "refresh": 2,
        "current": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is the door there",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Time since the last successful open",
      "description": "The 3am panel. postern_gate_last_open_timestamp_seconds moves only when a gate element was genuinely installed by the agent, after the firewall backend returned success. The SPA path never replies, so no client can prove the gate acted; this is the agent's own account of it. A host that has never opened one reports 0 here, which reads as a very large age and is the correct alarm.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 604800
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 2592000
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "time() - postern_gate_last_open_timestamp_seconds{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Health is the join",
      "description": "Hosts whose agent reports itself healthy while the external probe cannot reach it — design section 8's most valuable state, and the one that makes a break-glass door useless on the day it is needed. Computed by postern:health_join_red:host_id in dashboards/rules.yml, which must be loaded for this panel to have data: the probe is a client role and does not run on the host, so the two halves arrive from two scrape targets and are joined on the host_id enrollment issued. Anything above zero is a page.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "count(postern:health_join_red:host_id == 1) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "hosts the probe cannot reach that call themselves healthy",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Agent self-assessment",
      "description": "The two halves are independent by construction: agent_up is the live renewal signal and goes green again the moment a renewal succeeds; standing is a condition — a reverted transaction, an unusable replay store — that a later successful renewal has no business clearing. inert means a global pre-arm precondition failed, so no gate can be opened and the SPA port is silent.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 1,
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_agent_health_red{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} red ({{source}})"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_agent_inert{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} inert"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Gate state",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sources currently admitted",
      "description": "A count per service and per source kind. Deliberately not a list of addresses: which addresses are admitted through a break-glass gate is close to who is logged in from where, and a label per address would also be an unbounded series on a root daemon. An asserted source is an operator-supplied CIDR, so it is a wider hole than an observed one and is broken out for that reason.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_gate_open_sources{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} {{service}} ({{source_kind}})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Services armed by pre-arm",
      "description": "0 means pre-arm disabled exactly this service and left every other gate, the SPA listener and agent_up alone. A knock for a disabled service is refused by the agent rather than punched into rules that were never armed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 1,
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_gate_service_armed{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} {{service}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Opens and open failures",
      "description": "An authorized knock the firewall backend refused is a failed open: the operator got no reply either way, because the SPA path never sends one, so this panel is the only place that difference is visible.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance, service) (increase(postern_gate_opens_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} {{service}} opened"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance, service) (increase(postern_gate_open_failures_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} {{service}} FAILED"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "SPA",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "SPA rates",
      "description": "Every datagram the packet loop finished with, split by outcome. A rising rate of undecryptable packets means the SPA port has been found; design section 8 counts these rather than logging one row each, because at the kernel's 20/second limit a record per rejection is roughly 1.7 million rows a day.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(postern_spa_datagrams_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} handled"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance, service) (rate(postern_spa_accepted_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} accepted {{service}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(postern_spa_rejections_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "rejected: {{reason}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Clock skew",
      "description": "Difference between the host's clock and the timestamp inside an authenticated packet. The band between freshness_window (60s) and freshness_window_max (24h) is the one that matters: a host drifting in there keeps admitting gate packets, because the counter path carries them, and stops accepting actions entirely. The p99 line is the distribution; the signed line says which way.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 60
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 86400
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (instance, le) (rate(postern_spa_clock_skew_seconds_bucket{instance=~\"$instance\"}[1h])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} p99 |skew|"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_spa_clock_skew_last_seconds{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} last (signed)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(postern_spa_clock_skew_seconds_sum{instance=~\"$instance\"}[1h])) / sum by (instance) (rate(postern_spa_clock_skew_seconds_count{instance=~\"$instance\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} mean |skew|"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Packets admitted by the counter path alone",
      "description": "A gate packet whose timestamp was already outside freshness_window and which only the replay counter admitted. Non-zero here is a host whose clock has drifted past 60s but not past 24h — it still works, and nothing else in the system says so. Read alongside the too_old rejections, which are the same drift past the hard bound.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (increase(postern_spa_accepted_beyond_freshness_window_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} counter path only"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (increase(postern_spa_rejections_total{instance=~\"$instance\",reason=\"too_old\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} past freshness_window_max"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "agent_up renewals, and whether the SPA port is actually open",
      "description": "The renewal counter says the call succeeded. The lease line says the call had an effect — they are not the same thing, and for a long time they disagreed silently: a re-add of a live element with an identical ttl is ignored by the kernel, so every renewal 'succeeded', the dead-man lapsed on a fixed clock, and the SPA port went silent while this dashboard stayed green. Seconds-until-silent at or below zero means no knock can reach the host right now.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance, result) (rate(postern_agent_up_renewals_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} {{result}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "time() - postern_agent_up_last_success_timestamp_seconds{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} age of last success"
        },
        {
          "expr": "postern_agent_up_expires_timestamp_seconds{instance=~\"$instance\"} - time()",
          "legendFormat": "seconds until the SPA port goes silent",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Probe and deploys",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Canary streak and the age of the last proof",
      "description": "The probe's own view. reason is the distinction the exit code cannot draw: gate_not_closed means the canary port answers with no gate open — a host with no drop rule at all, which `postern open` reports as healthy — while gate_not_opened means the gate is shut and the knock did not reach it. A host that has never passed reports an age of decades here, on purpose.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "postern_probe_consecutive_failures",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} consecutive failures",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (host, reason) (increase(postern_probe_sweeps_total{verdict=\"fail\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{reason}}",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "time() - postern_probe_last_pass_timestamp_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} since last proof",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Probe verdict per host",
      "description": "An enumeration, not a number: every state has a series on every host, so state=\"red\" is 0 on a healthy host rather than absent. That is what lets an alert tell a green host from a probe that has stopped reporting, and it is why unknown — nothing has ever been measured — cannot be read as a value on the same scale as green.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 30
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "postern_probe_health",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{state}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Confirm-or-revert",
      "description": "An armed configuration reverts unless a bound confirm arrives before the deadline. A pending transaction that stays pending is a deploy nobody finished; a revert is a deploy that took the host somewhere it could not be confirmed from.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 30
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_transaction_pending{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} pending"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_transaction_deadline_timestamp_seconds{instance=~\"$instance\"} - time()",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} seconds to the dead-man"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (increase(postern_transaction_reverts_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} reverts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Builds, uptime, and the join key",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_agent_info{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "time() - postern_agent_start_timestamp_seconds{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "expr": "postern_probe_target_info",
          "legendFormat": "probe target",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "description": "host_id is what makes the probe's series and the agent's joinable without an operator hand-writing a matching label into their scrape config. It appears on postern_agent_info from the host and on postern_probe_target_info from the probe; if a host is missing from one of them, the join above silently covers fewer hosts than you think."
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Fleet bundle pull",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Bundle pulls: applied, rejected, and running version",
      "description": "The hub is a management convenience: a rejection here means this host kept the last good policy it already had, never that the packet path stopped working. A rising rejections_total against a flat applied_total is a hub this fleet is not receiving updates from. applied_version is the version this host is actually running; a host stuck below the fleet's current version is refusing bundles, which a throttled rejection log alone would not surface.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (increase(postern_bundle_pull_applied_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} applied"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance, reason) (increase(postern_bundle_pull_rejections_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} rejected: {{reason}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "postern_bundle_applied_version{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} running version"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Fleet heartbeat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 51
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Heartbeats sent and rejected",
      "description": "The hub is a management convenience: a rejection here means the hub does not currently have a fresh view of this host, never that the packet path stopped working. A rising rejections_total against a flat sent_total is a hub this host cannot currently reach.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 52
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (increase(postern_heartbeat_sent_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} sent"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (instance, reason) (increase(postern_heartbeat_rejections_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} rejected: {{reason}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
